FAQ = [
 ("What is the best bed rack for a 2019+ Silverado 1500?",
  "For a rooftop tent, the Putco Venture TEC. Putco rates it at 1,000 lb static, 600 lb dynamic and 300 lb off-road, it mounts to the stake pockets without drilling, and Putco lists versions for the T1's 5'8\" and 6'6\" beds. If that price is too much, the RealTruck GoRack carries the same 1,000 lb static and 600 lb dynamic figures for $1,089.99 at RealTruck, and its Amazon listing names the 2019–2024 Silverado 1500 and Sierra 1500 short bed."),
 ("Do 2014–2018 Silverado bed racks fit the 2019+ truck?",
  "Not reliably. The 2019 T1 Silverado has a new bed, and some listings still say \"2014 & up\" or \"2014–2023\" because a rack family spans both trucks. Putco's own site lists 2019+ versions separately, so match the part to your model year. Watch for the 2019 Silverado LD as well: it is the old truck sold alongside the new one, and it takes 2014–2018 parts. The 2022 LTD is a T1 and takes 2019+ parts."),
 ("Which bed length do I have on my Silverado 1500?",
  "The T1 has three beds: short (69.9 in at the floor, Crew Cab only), standard (79.4 in, Double Cab and Crew Cab) and long (98.2 in, Regular Cab). Retailers call the short bed 5'8\" or 5'10\" and the standard bed 6'6\" or 6'7\". It is the same bed under two labels. Rough Country, for example, says its rack does not fit 6'7\" beds, meaning the standard bed."),
 ("Can I run a tonneau cover with a bed rack on the Silverado?",
  "Yes, if you pick them together. Stake-pocket racks such as the Putco Venture TEC and Adarac Pro Series stand clear of inside-the-rail roll-up covers; Putco says most inside-rail roll-ups work, and Agri-Cover lists ACCESS roll-ups and LOMAX folding covers. The GoRack can mount on T-slot covers. Rough Country says its rack won't fit tri-fold covers. BackRack sells separate tonneau hardware kits for its headache racks."),
 ("What do static and dynamic ratings mean for a rooftop tent?",
  "Dynamic is the load the rack can carry while the truck moves, when bumps and braking multiply forces. Static is the parked figure, which matters when people sleep in the tent. Putco and RealTruck rate their racks at 1,000 lb static and 600 lb dynamic, Adarac at 1,000 lb static and 500 lb dynamic, and Rough Country at 750 lb static and 400 lb dynamic. Keep the tent and gear under the dynamic number when driving."),
 ("Does a bed rack block the Multi-Flex tailgate?",
  "No. Racks mount to the stake pockets or bed rails, and the tailgate stays free, so the main gate drops and the Multi-Flex inner gate and step still work. GM rates that step at 375 lb. The things to check are a tonneau's rear panel, which can sit over the inner gate when closed, and any rack with rear uprights that stick out past the bed. Measure clearance before loading long boards."),
 ("Will a full-height rack cover the third brake light?",
  "It can, depending on crossbar height and what you carry. The T1's third brake light sits at the top of the cab's rear, and a crossbar or tent at cab height can block the view of it from following cars. A mid-height rack keeps the load lower. Check the light from behind the truck after loading, and remember a tent overhanging the cab also sits in that line."),
 ("Can a bed rack go on a Silverado with factory storage boxes?",
  "Usually not. GM's in-bed side storage boxes sit along the rails where clamps and uprights go, and none of the racks here list them as supported. BackRack's toolbox hardware kits are for aftermarket crossover toolboxes, not the factory side boxes. If your truck has them, ask the rack maker before ordering, or choose a headache rack at the front of the bed."),
 ("Is a headache rack the same as a bed rack?",
  "No. A headache rack such as the BackRack Original bolts across the front of the bed to guard the rear window and carry lights. RealTruck lists it at $239.99 in 12-gauge steel. It gives you one front tie-point for ladders or lumber, and you can pair it with a rear rack. It won't carry a rooftop tent. A full bed rack spans the bed and carries the load across both axles."),
 ("How much does a bed rack add to Silverado payload?",
  "The rack's own weight comes out of payload before any gear. Yakima lists its OverHaul HD towers at 59.52 lb before crossbars. Add the tent, recovery gear and passengers, then check the payload figure on your door-jamb sticker, which varies by cab, engine and trim. Trail Boss and ZR2 trucks have their own sticker figures, so read yours rather than a brochure number before loading a heavy tent."),
]

